From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-mtk: quiesce before OS handoff

The MediaTek xHCI driver implements remove() to deregister the controller
and power down the host IP, but driver model does not call it before
booting an OS because the driver lacks DM_FLAG_OS_PREPARE.  This can leave
the controller performing DMA after Linux has reused U-Boot's memory.

Mark the driver for removal during OS preparation, matching xhci-pci.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
index f16b59c84c..c73d721c9b 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
@@ -364,6 +364,6 @@ U_BOOT_DRIVER(usb_xhci) = {
 	.remove = xhci_mtk_remove,
 	.ops = &xhci_usb_ops,
 	.bind = dm_scan_fdt_dev,
 	.priv_auto	= sizeof(struct mtk_xhci),
-	.flags = DM_FLAG_ALLOC_PRIV_DMA,
+	.flags = DM_FLAG_ALLOC_PRIV_DMA | DM_FLAG_OS_PREPARE,
 };
